{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":49790,"duration_api_ms":49714,"num_turns":9,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"047f65ae-3dfd-4094-8f60-0d9d4c43d993","total_cost_usd":0.30385175000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26655,"cache_read_input_tokens":187396,"output_tokens":1741,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26655,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":1741,"cacheReadInputTokens":187396,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26655,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30385175000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All three amendments verified against the source code. Each identifies a real defect: (1) missing alk_budget decrement after comammox is an inconsistency bug with the code's own documented intent, (2) silent zero-volume in migration produces corrupt water state, (3) TUI load path bypasses migration-aware SaveFile::from_json causing incorrect stability tracker initialization for legacy saves.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-a8d59226","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: at line 273, do_budget is decremented by comammox_o2_cost, and comammox_alk_cost is computed at line 272, but alk_budget is never decremented. This directly contradicts the comment at line 270 ('Debit shared budgets for comammox') and breaks symmetry with the AOB pattern at lines 218-219 where both do_budget and alk_budget are decremented. The NOB section (line 277 comment even says 'uses remaining DO/alk budget') currently only checks do_budget, but the stale alk_budget is a latent bug for any future guild added after comammox that checks alkalinity. The fix is a single safe line addition."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-8bd2540e","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: lines 214-216 use unwrap_or(0.0) for length, width, fill_height. If any is zero or missing, gross_volume_l = 0.0 at line 217, which triggers the else branch at line 236-237 setting scale = 0.0. This silently multiplies every dissolved total (ammonia, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DO, DIC, DOC, etc.) by zero, producing a 'valid' but chemically empty water state. A v2 save with malformed or missing geometry would appear to migrate successfully but lose all water chemistry data. This is a data-corruption path that should error or warn rather than silently zero everything."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-e30f07ff","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: line 237 uses serde_json::from_str::<SaveFile>(&raw) directly, bypassing SaveFile::from_json (line 117-121) which calls from_value with full migration chain, version validation, and stability_tracker reseeding. The damage path is clear: (1) serde_json::from_str deserializes stability_tracker via #[serde(default)] with all zeros, (2) post_load at line 239-241 sends this to the API, (3) has_serialized_stability_tracker sees the key exists and returns true, (4) reseed_stability_tracker_if_missing skips reseeding. Result: old saves get all-zero stability tracking instead of properly computed baselines. Additionally, any future migration or version check is completely bypassed for TUI-loaded files. The fix is straightforward: replace serde_json::from_str with SaveFile::from_json."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f649d447-c5a0-4f30-af03-63cfd1a0c060"}
